Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: Experimental faint screen-colored control spill locally qualified.
Dependencies: Existing framebuffer-derived ScreenIllumination.

Purpose
-------
With lamp and room lights off, let LCD light barely reveal nearby controls
without brightening the whole room or changing the existing table pool.
User explicitly calls this an experiment and may ask to remove it.

Tasks
-----
[x] Reuse existing smoothed native LCD color/brightness, not new sampling.
[x] Add isolated weak reflected fill attached to the screen transform.
[x] Keep D-pad, A/B, Start/Select and shoulder controls faint, not emissive.
[x] Clear on a black framebuffer and power off.
[x] Preserve primary LCD table emission and existing button behavior.
[x] Review bounded actual play/Inspect captures.
[ ] Publish through the unchanged full gate and independently verify live behavior.
[x] Record experiment scope and precise removal boundary.

Acceptance criteria
-------------------
Actual rendered controls are faintly visible with only the LCD on, follow
screen color/brightness and go dark on black/off. The room remains dark and
the original table illumination remains. No ambient-light increase, glowing
button materials, new frame sampler, extra render loop or emulator change.
This is an artistic first-bounce approximation, not physical ray tracing.

Completion evidence
-------------------
The existing forward-facing LCD area light cannot illuminate coplanar caps.
Add one reverse-facing local RectAreaLight, controlSpill, at LCD-localz1.2,
twice viewport width/height. Reuse the same smoothed linear sample and color;
peak*.1 intensity versus unchanged peak*120 primary emission. No shadow map.
Eight product lines in src/lighting.js. Initial gain2 overlights caps; narrow
dimmed fill leaves shoulders too dark. Wider/weaker final fill balances them.
Baseline regression reads D-pad0/255 with a full-white native framebuffer and
fails visibility. Final actual GPU probes read approximate max RGB:
D-pad23, A18.32, B24, Start24, Select22, leftshoulder5.68/rightshoulder5.4.
All stay below35/255 even at full-white maximum; black and power-off probes
remain below1. Red/blue transfer and unchanged table pool within1/255 pass.
Syntax/build/12units and three native/browser lighting/control cases pass46.7s.
Actual full-white worst-case play and Inspect captures reviewed; these are
controlled paused-native fixtures, not the user's supplied ROM/screenshots.
Existing published lcd-light/dark-power-off figures restored byte-for-byte
after the historical integration test generated its usual temporary captures.
No README media regeneration, private-ROM/audio test or human acceptance.

Removal boundary
----------------
Remove only controlSpill construction, clear and update lines in
src/lighting.js plus this experiment's dedicated browser regression/docs.
Keep the original forward emitter, framebuffer sampling, table lighting,
native runtime and the separate fullscreen-resume fix intact.

Completion log
--------------
2026-11-05: User requests barely visible controls with all lights off; explicitly
experimental and reversible. Local effect and actual rendered bounds qualified.
